1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lakshmi (Sanskrit: लक्ष्मी, lakṣmī, ˈləkʂmiː) is the Hindu goddess of wealth, fortune and prosperity. She is the wife and shakti (energy) of Vishnu, a major god in Hinduism.[2] Lakshmi is also an important deity in
2 CONC  Jainism and found in Jain temples,[3] as well as on the oldest surviving stupas and cave temples of Buddhism.[4] In Buddhist sects of Tibet, Nepal and southeast Asia, goddess Vasudhara mirrors the characteristics and attributes o
2 CONC f the Hindu goddess Lakshmi with minor iconographic differences.[5]
