2 CONT Shani is a deity in medieval era texts, who is considered inauspicious and is feared for delivering misfortune and loss to those who deserve it.[15] He is also capable of conferring boons and blessings to the worthy, depending upo
2 CONC n their karma. In medieval Hindu literature, he is inconsistently referred to as the son of Sun and Chhaya (shadow), or as the son of Balarama and Revati.[3][16] His alternate names include Ara, Kona and Kroda.[3] As per the Hindu
2 CONC  texts,'peepal' or fig tree is the abode of Shani (while other texts associate the same tree with Vasudeva).[17]
