2 CONT Sons of Sharmishtha Druhyu and his descendants, the Bhoj Vansha, are believed to have formed the Twipra Kingdom.[3] Anu gave rise to a Mleccha tribe, Tusharas (Tukharas), with their kingdom located in the north west of India as pe
2 CONC r the epic Mahabharata. (Mbh 1:85) Further on Kekaya, a warrior on the Pandava side into whose chariot Bhima got during the fighting on the sixth day. As per Bhagavata Purana the Usinaras, the Sibi, the Madras, and the Kekayas wer
