2 CONT Horse-keeping: Nakula's deep understanding of horse breeding and training is documented in the Mahabharata after the death of Narakasura by Krishna. In a conversation with Virata, Nakula claimed to know the art of treating all ill
2 CONC nesses of horses.[11][12] Astrology: Nakula was a great astrologer, but he could say something about the future just once, after which he used to forget what he had said. Before the epic Mahabharta War started, Duryodhana approach
2 CONC ed Nakula asking him who would win the war. Nakula replied that the army of the one could can hoist his flag on the stone of a mountain would win the war. As soon as he said this to Duryodhana, he forgot what he had said, but Bhee
2 CONC ma heard it. Duryodhana sent his army and men to hoist a flag at a particular mountain. Bheema ran alone. Duryodhana's men were able to reach the mountain before Bheema could. Bheema fought them and put a few of them down, but he 
2 CONC had forgotten to carry the flag of his side. He was clad only in his underclothes ('Gerua'), which he hoisted as his side's flag.[citation needed] Ayurveda: Being a son of the physicians, Ashwini Kumaras, Nakula was also believed 
2 CONC to be an expert in Ayurveda.[13]kula (Sanskrit: नकुल, Nakula),is a protagonist of the epic Mahabharata. He is the son of the Goddess of Madri, Kunti's brother-in-law. He is the twin brother Sahadeva and was considered the son of g
2 CONC od Aswin, healer god of twins. According to the Mahabharata, Nakula was very handsome and very good-looking. According to Dropadi, Nakula was the most handsome man in the world. However, the vices of Nakula is proud of its good lo
2 CONC oks. This was disclosed by Yudistira in Prasthanikaparwa book.
2 CONT
2 CONT Literally, the word Nakula in Sanskrit refers to the color of ichneumon, a kind of rat or rodent from Egypt. Nakula also can mean "mink", or it can also mean "rat Bengal". Nakula is also another name of Lord Shiva.
2 CONT
2 CONT NAKULA IN MAHABHARATA  According to the Mahabharata, the twins Nakula and Sahadeva have special abilities in caring for horses and cattle. Nakula is described as being very comforting. He is also meticulous in carrying out their d
2 CONC uties and always keep an eye on her sister's mischievous nature, Bima, and even against what seemed a serious joke. Nakula also have proficiency in playing the sword weapon. When the Pandavas suffered exile in the forest, the four
2 CONC th Pandava (Bhima, Arjuna, Nakula, Sahadeva) died from drinking poisoned water from a lake. When a figure unseen spirits give an opportunity to Yudhisthira to choose one of four brothers to be revived, Nakula was the one chosen by
2 CONC  Yudhishthira to live again. This is because Nakula was the son of Madri, and Yudhisthira, who is the son of Kunti, to be fair to both the mother. If he chose the Milky or Arjuna, it is no longer the son of Madri who will continue
2 CONC  the descent. When the Pandavas had to undergo the incognito in the kingdom of Virata, Nakula horse disguised as a nurse under the pseudonym "Grantika". Nakula to participate in the great battle of Kurukshetra, and won the big war
