1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 	Druhyu and his descendant are believed to have formed the Twipra Kingdom.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Druhyu The Druhyus were a people of Ancient India. They are already mentioned in the Rigveda.[16] They lived in the Ghandara region. They were often considered to be Dasyus. The Puranas say that they moved north and west, and then
2 CONC  settled in Gandhara, Aratta (northwest Punjab) and Setu. (VP IV.17) The Druhyus were driven out of the land of the seven rivers by Mandhatrand their next king Ghandara settled in a north-western region which became known as Ghand
2 CONC ara. The sons of the later Druhyu king Pracetas finally migrate to the region north of Afghanistan.( Bhagavata 9.23.15-16; Visnu 4.17.5; Vayu 99.11-12; Brahmanda 3.74.11-12 and Marsya 48.9.) Some scholars say they could be related
2 CONC  to Zoroastrian, Iranian, Greek or European peoples. They were probably a north-western people[17]. In the Hindu epics, they are connected withGhandara.[18]
