1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In Hindu mythology, '''Yashoda''' (Yaśodā; संस्कृत: यशोदा), also spelt as Yasodha, is the foster-mother of Lord Krishna and wife of Nanda. She is described in the Puranic texts of Hinduism. According to Bhagavata P
2 CONC urana, Krishna was born to Devaki, but Krishna's father Vasudeva brought the newborn Krishna to Nanda Baba in Gokul, in order to raise and protect Krishna from Devaki's brother Kansa, the king of Mathura. The name Yashoda means 'o
2 CONC ne who is giver (da, दा) of Fame (Yash, यश)'
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yashoda
2 CONT
2 CONT Yasoda played an important role in raising Krishna (Krushn)'s elder brother Balarama (son of Vasudeva and Rohini). Later she had a daughter of her own named as Ekānaṅgā.
