2 CONT '''Shrutakarma'''[14](IAST: Śrutakarmā, Sanskrit: श्रुतकर्मा, lit. he whose deeds are famous) or Shrutakirti (IAST: '''Śrutakīrti''', Sanskrit: श्रुतकीर्ति, lit. he whose fame is heard about) was the son born to Arjuna and Draupad
2 CONC i,[15] the youngest of the Upapandavas. He had two sisters, Pragya and Pragathi (twin daughters). His horses were supposed to bear the colour of kingfishers.[16] He was a capable archer like his father. He fought against Dushasana
2 CONC  and Ashwathama in the battle. He killed King Chitrasena, another king of Abhisara, on the 16th day.[17][18]
