2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Drupada (Sanskrit: द्रुपद, lit. firm-footed or pillar[1]), also known as Yagnasena (Sanskrit: यज्ञसेन, lit. father of Draupadi), is a character in the Mahābhārata. The son of King Prishata, he was the king of the land of Southern 
2 CONC Panchala.[2] His capital was known as Kampilya.[3]
2 CONT
