1 NOTE {geni:about_me} NOBLE SON OF DHRITARASHTRA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Yuyutsu was the only son of Dhritarashtra who survived the Kurukshetra war.He was one among the 11 Athirathis (capable of fighting 10,000 warriors at a time) among the Kauravas. Yuyutsu, Duryodhana's half-brother, fought battle on
2 CONC  behalf of Pandavas.Just before the battle of Kurukshetra between Kauravas and Pandavas, when asked if any one wanted to change sides in the battle, Yuyutsu changes his side from Kauravas to Pandavas. When Pandavas won the war, as
2 CONC  a token of gratitude, the eldest Pandava Yudhisthira granted the kingship of Indraprastha to Yuyutsu, one among the 10 warriors survived in Mahabharatha war.
2 CONT
2 CONT Yuyutsu (Sanskrit: युयुत्सू) in the Hindu epic Mahabharata was a son of Dhritrashtra with a Vaishya woman named Sauvali.[1] He was younger than Duryodhana and elder than the rest of the ninety-nine Kuru brothers and Dushala. Event
2 CONC ually, he was the only son of Dhritarashtra who survived the Kurukshetra war. After the war, he took charge as the King of Indraprastha. Contents  [hide]  1 Birth 2 Spy in the Kaurava camp 3 During Kurukshetra War 4 After the War 
2 CONC 5 Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT Fearing problems with Gandhari's pregnancy which had continued for over a year, Dhritrashtra married Sauvali, a woman from Vaishya Varna, from whom he bore a son, Yuyutsu. Yuyutsu was born younger to Duryodhana, but elder to Dusha
2 CONC sana, other Kauravas and Dussala. Thus, contrary to popular perception, Dhritrashtra had 101 sons.[2] The Mahabharatha cites the following other names for Yuyutsu: Dhartarstra, Dhrtarastraja, Dhrtarastraputra, Karana, Kauravya, an
2 CONC d Vaisyaputra.[3] [edit]Spy in the Kaurava camp
2 CONT
2 CONT Yuyutsu played a major role in the Mahabharatha as a spy among the Kauravas. He assisted the Pandavas by providing critical information about Kauravas' preparation and planning. He also saved the life of Bhima by informing the Pan
2 CONC davas about Duryodhana's cunning schemes, which included poisoning water.[4][5] [edit]During Kurukshetra War
2 CONT
2 CONT Before the onset of the battle of Kurukshetra War between Kauravas and Pandavas, Yuyutsu shifts from Kauravas to the Pandava camp. Yuyutsu fought the battle on the side of the Pandavas. He was one among the 11 Athirathis (capable 
2 CONC of fighting 10,000 warriors at a time) among the Kauravas. Yuyutsu was one among the 10 warriors to have survived the war.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT After the war, Yuyutsu was appointed as the guardian to King Parikshit of Hastinapur when the Pandavas departed for the Himalayas after the war.[7][8] When the Pandavas headed for heavenly abode at the start of the Kali Yuga, Yudh
2 CONC isthira granted the kingship of Indraprastha to Yuyutsu.
