1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Summary
2 CONT
2 CONT Shakuni (Sanskrit: शकुनि) also known as Saubala, was the prince of Gandhar and one of the main villians in the Hindu epic Mahabharata. He was the brother of Gandhari and hence Duryodhana's maternal uncle. He is believed to be an e
2 CONC xtremely intelligent but devious man. Shakuni is often credited as the mastermind behind the Mahabharata war. Shakuni had two sons named Uluka and Vrikaasur. Shakuni was born in Gandhar in modern day Afghanistan to King Subala. He
2 CONC  was a great devotee of Lord Shiva. It is believed that Shakuni was unhappy with his sister Gandhari's marriage with blind Kuru prince Dhritarashtra. He was more so ever angry with Bhishma for bringing this proposal as he found it
2 CONC  insulting and demeaning. He swore to avenge this insult by slowly destroying Bhishma's clan. He achieved this by poisoning the mind of his volatile nephew, and influenced Duryodhana into instigating the war with the Pandavas, whi
2 CONC ch resulted in the destruction of the Kauravas. Thus, he is seen by many as the ultimate cause of the Kurukshetra War .. His hatred for Bhishma became more deeper when Bhishma chose eldest Pandava Yudhisthira as the next successor
2 CONC  to the throne. He felt that this was an unfair decision and believed that Duryodhana his nephew should have been the rightful heir to the throne. [edit]Role in the Mahabharat Shakuni is often depicted as a man dressed in black cl
2 CONC othes, sporting a white beard, wearing a half- kireetam, rubbing dice in his hands often, and limping slightly while walking. Shakuni was most importantly the mastermind of the Mahabharata war. It was because of his sinister plans
2 CONC  that culminated into the biggest wars in Indian mythological history. He was an evil genius who was so shrewd to see through things and confident of his skills to undo the opponents. Though his designs to destroy the Pandava's fa
2 CONC iled one by one, he was still unshaken in his faith to destroy the lineage of Bhishma. He played on the virtues of the Pandava's themselves, to bring problems of serious nature. His main objective was to instigate Duryodhana again
2 CONC st the Pandava's, whether it was advising Duryodhana to mix the Kalakoota poison into Bheema's food or hiring Purochana to kill the Pandavas in the house of wax most famously known as Lakshagraha. An evil plotter he also secretly 
2 CONC wanting the great sage Durvasa to curse the Pandava's in anger, he asked the sage to visit the Pandava's in the forest after Draupadi had eaten her meal, knowing that the Pandavas would then have nothing to feed him. During the Ku
2 CONC rukshetra war he was the one who hatched the plan to kill Arjuna's son Abhimanyu by cheating and breaking the war protocol. However Shakuni is perhaps best known for masterminding the infamous Game of Dice between the Kaurava's an
2 CONC d the Pandava's. A master of sorcery, it is said the dice used by Shakuni's were made from his father's thigh bones and hence generated any desired number. Unaware of this fact the Pandava's were defeated in the gambling match, an
2 CONC d which eventually led to the war at Kurukshetra and subsequent destruction of the Kuru clan. [During the Game of Dice episode in the Mahabharata, the youngest of the Pandava brothers Sahadeva had taken an oath to avenge Draupadi'
2 CONC s insult and swore to kill Shakuni the mastermind of the episode. As sworn, Shakuni was killed by Sahadeva on the seventeenth day of the Kurukshetra war.
2 CONT
2 CONT SAKUNI'S FATHER SAID THAT EVEN THOUGH HE DID NOT LEAVE A VAST KINGDOM.  HE HAS GIVEN HIM  A TOOL WITH WHICH HE CAN GET KINGDOMS.  BY  DICE GAMBLING
2 CONT
2 CONT WHEN HE PASSES AWAY  HIS ANKLE BONES  WILL NOT  BURN   AND WILL NOT BECOME ASH AFTER CREMATION. HE CAN PICK UP THE ANKLE BONE AND MAKE DICE. AND USE IT WHEN HE PLAYS AND WHATEVER NO HE WANTS HE WILL GET WHEN THE DICE IS CAST IN GA
2 CONC MB. GAME.HE OBEYED HIS FATHERS INSTRUCTIONS
2 CONT   AND MADE DICE AND    PLAYED .  THIS GAVE HIM COMPLETE VICTORY  IN DICE GAME WITH DHARMA PUTRA.  WHO LOST EVERYTHING EVENTUALLY.
