2 CONT In Hindu scriptures, Bharata (Sanskrit: भरत, Bharata i.e., "The cherished") is a legendary emperor and the founder of the Bhārata dynasty and thus an ancestor of the Pandavas and the Kauravas in the Sanskrit epic Mahabharata. Thou
2 CONC gh the Bhāratas are a prominent tribe in the Rigveda the story of Bharata is first told in the Adi Parva of the Mahabharata, wherein he is the son of Dushyanta and Shakuntala The story of his parents and his birth is also related 
2 CONC in Kalidasa's famous play Abhijñānashākuntala.
2 CONT
2 CONT India has been called Bharatavarṣa (the country of Bharata) after him and Bhārat is an official name of the Republic of India.
