1 NAME Yamunamuni /Alavandar/
2 GIVN Yamunamuni
2 _MARNM Alavandar
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 918
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1038
1 OCCU Writer, ruler, debator, saint of Srivaishnava tradition
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Authored 8 books in Sanskrit on Hindu religion and Philosophy:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Gitaartha Sangraha (Essence of Bhagavad-Gita)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Stotra Ratna (Devtional hymn to VishNu)
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. PurushanirNayam
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Chatushloki
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Agama PramaaNa
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Atma Siddhi
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Samvita Siddhi
2 CONT
2 CONT 9. Ishwara Siddhi
2 CONT
2 CONT Won half the kingdom and earned the title "ALavandaar" by defeating the royal priest in a debate at King Chola's assembly. The royal priest was unable to refute the three questions raised as part of the debate.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Queen is barren (queen had only one child. Having only child is like "barren" in the Hindu concept)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Queen had other husbands (Soma, Gandharva and Agni are the previous husbands for every girl, and the groom she eventually weds is the fourth husband)
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. King is not without faults (King has a share of  faults of his subjects)
