1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sangrama_Vijayottunggavarman Wikipedia]Ruled from 1064 to 1169.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sangrama Vijayottunggavarman (spelled alternatively as Sangramavijayottunggavarman or Sang Rama Wijaya Tungga Warman) was an emperor of Srivijaya of Sailendra dynasty, who reigned in the early 11th century in Kadaram and succeeded
2 CONC  Mara Vijayottunggavarman. He is best known for being captured by the Chola Navy following the Cholan invasion of Srivijaya.
2 CONT
2 CONT The name of the emperor was inscribed on an inscription dated 1030 CE in Rajarajeshwaram Temple, Tanjore. The inscription was made during the reign of Rajendra Chola I, to commemorate his military campaign against Srivijaya that w
2 CONC as launched in 1025. The inscription states that the Cholas successfully sacked Kadaram and took a large amount of treasures, including the Vidhyadara-torana, the jewelled 'war gate' of Srivijaya adorned with great splendour. Duri
2 CONC ng the raid of Kadaram, Vijayatunggavarman was captured.
