1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ratu Talaga abt 1420 - 1450.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes on May 18, 2009:
2 CONT
2 CONT Her name in Joyce FG: Ratu Simbarkencana, link to her other profile:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.geni.com/people/Ratu-Simbarkencana/6000000003011209031
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Also known as Raden Dewi Simbarkancana. During her reign in the 14th century, Islam was beginning to spread by Moslem Santris (teachers) from Cirebon. The center of the kingdom was moved to the Northern side of Talaga, in Walangsu
2 CONC ji near Buniasih village. When she passed away, her reign was succeeded by her son, Sunan Parung   Raden Dewi Simbarkancana 
2 CONT
2 CONT She had the leadership qualities of her father, Prabu Talagamanggung. She married Palembanggunung, Kingdom Advisor. She did not know in the beginning that the death of her father was because he was murdered by her husband. But as 
2 CONC she found out, she murdered her own husband and took over the reign from her husband and continued with her father's legacy
2 CONT
2 CONT In regards to the father's murder by her own husband, she was said to be extremely sad because of two things:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. She felt betrayed by her own husband 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Because the father died in a tragedy.
2 CONT
2 CONT She wrote that "who on this earth would not be so sad when her father dies" and "betrayed by someone who was given a status, and yet paid back that kindness by murder". 
2 CONT
2 CONT Raden Dewi Simbarkancana married Raden Kusumalaya (Raden Palinggih) of Galuh Kingdom, son of Prabu Ningrat Kancana. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was known to be someone who is skilled both outside and inside, a healer and a strategist. She quelled the underground movements of Palembang Gunung's followers, and brought everything back under control, and the kingdom becam
2 CONC e stable and strong. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Her marriage to Raden Kusumalaya, there were 8 children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     1. Sunan Parung (Batara Sukawayana);
2 CONT
2 CONT     2. Sunan Cihaur, (Mangkurat Mangkureja);
2 CONT
2 CONT     3. Sunan Gunung Bungbulang;
2 CONT
2 CONT     4. Sunan Cengal (Kerok Batok);[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT     5. Sunan Jero Kaso;
2 CONT
2 CONT     6. Sunan Kuntul Putih;
2 CONT
2 CONT     7. Sunan Ciburang; dan
2 CONT
2 CONT     8. Sunan Tegalcau.
2 CONT
2 CONT She moved the kingdom from tutugan Gunung Ciremay to Walangsuji, in Desa Kagok, Kemantren Banjaran, the current Kecamatan Talaga.
2 CONT
2 CONT She governed there in Walangsuji for 7 years and 3 months. They reasoned that Walangsuji was not strategic enough to be the center of the kingdom, and hence it moved again. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The second move was to Parung
2 CONT
2 CONT When Ratu Simbarkancana died, Talaga Kingdom was taken by her son, titled Sunan Parung (1450 M). When he died, he was succeeded by his only daughter, Ratu Dewi Sunyalarang (1500 M) who was known by the title of Queen of Parung.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dewi Sunyalarang (Ratu Parung) married Raden Ragamantri, son of Prabu Mundingsari Ageung from Ratu Mayangkaruna. Raden Ragamantri is the grandson of  Begawan Garasiang and the grandson of Prabu Siliwangi II (Jaya Dewata or Pamanah
2 CONC  Rasa). 
2 CONT
2 CONT During the reign of Dewi Sunyalarang (Queen Parung), the center of the Kingdom was moved to Parung.
2 CONT
2 CONT One note ... history shows that women in our family does not necessarily play second class citizens. Yay !
